vulkan-systems
  gpu/       VulkanEngine resource ownership, staging, shaders, compute, culling
  render/    frame scheduling, image/geometry ownership, graph passes, draws
  bvh/       GPU radix LBVH, TLAS/BLAS instancing, triangle hits and refits
  spatial/   CPU BVH index and frustum queries
  network/   IPv4/IPv6 UDP, pinned DTLS 1.2 and reliable session
  jobs/      bounded multithreaded jobs and completion queue

Each module has a standalone build.c with C++17 APIs.
Root build.c exports VulkanSystems (gpu/render/bvh), VulkanSpatial, VulkanNetwork,
and VulkanJobs as independent static library targets. GPU and render depend
on VulkanEngine. Network and jobs do not depend on Vulkan.

Host initializes and shuts down the Vulkan device and swapchain.
No game-specific scene serialization, weapon logic, or authority rules live here.


VulkanSystems includes the bvh/ implementation; include <bvh/bvh.hpp> using
its bvh include directory. The standalone bvh/build.c target is for builds
that use only BVH; do not link both target libraries into the same executable.
The application compiles its BVH shader variants as it compiles render shaders.
No tools directory, GI implementation, fixed BRDF, or game-specific shading policy.
